# Architecture Overview — ${PROJECT_NAME} (Frontend React flavor)

> Stability: **stable**. Technical Single Source of Truth for this repo. Changes via ADR in `decisions/`.

## 1. Positioning

```
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|                    END USERS / OTHER FRONTENDS               |
+--------------------+-----------------------------------------+
                     |  HTTPS (user-facing API)
                     v
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|        ${SSOT_NAME} (separate solution)                       |
|   **SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH** — API-only                       |
|                                                              |
|   /api/...   /api/admin   <event broker>   <storage>          |
+--------------------+-----------------------------------------+
                     |  HTTPS (admin API only)
                     v
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|   ${PROJECT_NAME} (this repo)                                 |
|   React SPA  +  (optional) Fastify BFF                        |
|   Audience: ${PRIMARY_AUDIENCE}                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
                     ^
                     | desktop browser usage
                ADMIN OPERATORS
```

## 2. Responsibilities

### 2.1 ${SSOT_NAME}

Sole authority for: domain data, authentication, RBAC, policies, AI pipelines, ingest, storage, signed URLs, audit, job orchestration, schema versioning, token issuance, report generation.

### 2.2 This repo

Responsibilities = **presentation, UX orchestration, client-side form validation**.

- list/detail/form/dashboard rendering;
- composing admin API calls (read + mutation);
- server-state management (cache, invalidation, retry, controlled optimistic update);
- long-running job visualization (polling/SSE);
- user-error prevention (confirmations, schema validation, idempotency-key);
- cosmetic permission projection (hide/disable);
- accessibility, i18n, dark mode, dense UX.

**Does not** decide domain state. **Does not** duplicate logic. **Does not** bypass ${SSOT_NAME}.

### 2.3 Optional Fastify BFF

Introduced **only if** at least one of:

- httpOnly session cookie + CSRF (alternative to in-memory tokens);
- proxy with header rewriting for CORS in dev/prod;
- CSP nonce injection for static HTML;
- signed uploads (server-side delegation);
- secret stripping on sensitive endpoints.

The BFF carries **no domain logic**. Thin Fastify edge layer.

